{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25890072",
      "title": "Testing Connected Components",
      "sourceHash": "4aba5d0e63ec97d6fa10e6200e37fe8ee5b8b434aa883d815f074d3bd1a47bbe",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 4.25,
          "en": "Now let's continue writing tests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.25,
          "end": 8.51,
          "en": "and let's now explore how multiple components can interact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.51,
          "end": 10.86,
          "en": "with each other and how we can test that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.86,
          "end": 14.42,
          "en": "and how we can work with props and tests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.42,
          "end": 16.04,
          "en": "And for this, I'll stick to this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.04,
          "end": 18.79,
          "en": "very simple component I have here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.79,
          "end": 19.91,
          "en": "And what I want to do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.91,
          "end": 22.37,
          "en": "is now I want to create a new component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.37,
          "end": 24.6,
          "en": "the output component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.6,
          "end": 25.94,
          "en": "which does what the name implies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.94,
          "end": 28.66,
          "en": "It just outputs something.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 28.66,
          "end": 32.27,
          "en": "So this will be a quite straightforward component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.27,
          "end": 35.88,
          "en": "And of course I'm keeping it deliberately simple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 35.88,
          "end": 38.571,
          "en": "so that we can explore these basic testing concepts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.571,
          "end": 41.64,
          "en": "with basic examples.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.64,
          "end": 44.21,
          "en": "And the idea of this output component therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.21,
          "end": 47.03,
          "en": "is just to render a paragraph,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.03,
          "end": 50.27,
          "en": "which outputs props.children",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.27,
          "end": 55.27,
          "en": "or props.text, depending on how you want to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.43,
          "end": 58.13,
          "en": "And here I'll say props.children.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.13,
          "end": 61.06,
          "en": "And of course, this is kind of a redundant component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.06,
          "end": 63.79,
          "en": "but if we could have some extra styles on this paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.79,
          "end": 66.49,
          "en": "and then use this as kind of a wrapper component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.49,
          "end": 69.33,
          "en": "as we also sometimes did it in this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.33,
          "end": 72.07,
          "en": "for example, with that card component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.07,
          "end": 73.84,
          "en": "which we had in some projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 73.84,
          "end": 75.053,
          "en": "if you remember that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 76.1,
          "end": 80.013,
          "en": "So that's the output component and it does use props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.12,
          "end": 83.95,
          "en": "Now here, I got this greeting component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.95,
          "end": 86.19,
          "en": "and instead of rendering this paragraph here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.19,
          "end": 90.09,
          "en": "I now want to render my output component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.09,
          "end": 92.25,
          "en": "And let's see how that could work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 92.25,
          "end": 94.36,
          "en": "For this in this greeting component file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.36,
          "end": 99.277,
          "en": "I'll import output from dot slash output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.21000000000001,
          "end": 104.11,
          "en": "And now we can replace paragraph with output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.11,
          "end": 105.75,
          "en": "like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 105.75,
          "end": 108.083,
          "en": "and like that here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.65,
          "end": 111.66,
          "en": "Now, if I save everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.66,
          "end": 113.53999999999999,
          "en": "the nice thing which we'll notice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 113.53999999999999,
          "end": 117.69,
          "en": "is that the tests simply continue to work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.69,
          "end": 120.48,
          "en": "So that's the good thing about render",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.48,
          "end": 122.88,
          "en": "which we use to render the greeting component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.88,
          "end": 126.453,
          "en": "It really renders this entire component tree",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 126.453,
          "end": 128.63,
          "en": "that is required here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 128.63,
          "end": 131.85,
          "en": "So it renders not just greeting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 131.85,
          "end": 135.82,
          "en": "and ignores other components used in that JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 135.82,
          "end": 138.9,
          "en": "but it renders the content of those components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 138.9,
          "end": 142.32999999999998,
          "en": "like in this case, the output component as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 142.32999999999998,
          "end": 146.12,
          "en": "And technically we could therefore call this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 146.12,
          "end": 150.15,
          "en": "an integration test because now more than one unit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 150.15,
          "end": 152.59,
          "en": "more than one component is involved.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 152.59,
          "end": 156.21,
          "en": "But especially when dealing with such a wrapper component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 156.21,
          "end": 158.52,
          "en": "which doesn't have its own logic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 158.52,
          "end": 161.13,
          "en": "that's of course not really the right term.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.13,
          "end": 164.48,
          "en": "Testing the conjunction of these two components together",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.48,
          "end": 166.67000000000002,
          "en": "is absolutely fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 166.67000000000002,
          "end": 169.1,
          "en": "And that's why I wanted to show this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 169.1,
          "end": 171.21,
          "en": "This is not something that forces you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 171.21,
          "end": 174.09,
          "en": "to split your tests necessarily.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 174.09,
          "end": 176.01,
          "en": "You might want to split them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 176.01,
          "end": 179.47,
          "en": "if the output component becomes more complex",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 179.47,
          "end": 181.94,
          "en": "and also starts managing state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 181.94,
          "end": 184.61,
          "en": "then you might want to test that separately",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 184.61,
          "end": 187.31,
          "en": "from the core logic of the greeting component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 187.31,
          "end": 189.64,
          "en": "But since that is not the case here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 189.64,
          "end": 192.69,
          "en": "we definitely can keep the tests we have here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 192.69,
          "end": 197.113,
          "en": "in greeting test JS to keep testing as we did before.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}